    <!-- ============================================================================================
         ARMORY VEHICLE/SHIP RESEARCH-BUTTON HIDE (rule-9-safe, flag-gated).
         The 24 Armory vehicle/ship weapon+armor Level research buttons must be hidden for the HUMAN
         player (their levels now scale with the infantry research via libWoLU_SyncWeaponArmorLevels),
         while ENEMY Armories keep their vanilla buttons. Each node below ANDs the vanilla EFFECTIVE
         Show node (verbatim from the libertystory/liberty dependency chain) with WoLUNotCountFlag
         (NOT having WoLUnbalancedFlag). The human player HAS the flag → WoLUNotCountFlag is false →
         the AND is false → the button's Show fails → it is hidden. Enemy players never get the flag
         → WoLUNotCountFlag is true → the AND collapses to the vanilla node → vanilla behavior. This
         is the Shaped-Blast flag-gate pattern applied to a UI Show requirement; command cards are
         player-UI-only so enemies are untouched in effect (rule 9). The 24 CRequirement ids that
         point Show at these nodes are overridden in RequirementData.xml (same-id, merge-safe).
         CRequirementAnd operands are index-less <OperandArray value="..."/> entries (verified vanilla
         form, e.g. AndNotCountUpgradeTerranVehicleArmorsLevel1QueuedOrBetterNotCountUpgradeVanadium
         PlatingCompleteOnly in the libertystory reference). The vanilla operand node ids are all
         defined in the reference chain (confirmed by id-resolution sweep). ============================ -->

